  📗
    Whether a client that sent *header*, the value of an Accept-Encoding,
    takes gzip (RFC 9110, 12.5.3): it names gzip or x-gzip with a quality
    above nothing, or it names neither and takes everything (*) with a
    quality above nothing. A client that sent no such header, or an empty
    one, is taken to want the bytes as they are, and so is one whose quality
    for a coding cannot be read: the bytes as they are can be read by every
    client, and gzip only by one that takes it.
